mes>WJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prevalence of cerebral amyloid pathology in persons without dementia: a meta-analysis</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2015</year><volume>313</volume><fpage>1924</fpage><lpage>1938</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">25988462</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klunk</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Imaging brain amyloid in Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease with Pittsburgh Compound-B</article-title><source>Ann. Neurol.</source><year>2004</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>306</fpage><lpage>319</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14991808</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schwarz</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A large-scale comparison of cortical thickness and volume methods for measuring Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease severity</article-title><source>Neuroimage Clin.</source><year>2016</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>802</fpage><lpage>812</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">28050342</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Classification of amyloid-positivity in controls: comparison of visual read and quantitative approaches</article-title><source>Neuroimage</source><year>2013</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>215</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">23353602</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Silverman</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Wisniewski</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bobinski</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wegiel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Frequency of stages of Alzheimer-related lesions in different age categories</article-title><source>Neurobiol. Aging</source><year>1997</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>379</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9330965</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McLellan</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The Fifth Edition of the Addiction Severity Index</article-title><source>J. Subst. Abus. Treat.</source><year>1992</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>213</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maisto</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sobell</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sobell</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of two techniques to obtain retrospective reports of drinking behavior from alcohol abusers</article-title><source>Addict. Behav.</source><year>1982</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>38</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7080882</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Skinner H. &#x00026; Horn J. <italic>Alcohol Dependence Scale (ADS) User&#x02019;s Guide</italic> (Addiction Research Foundation, 1984).</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR19"><label>19.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Selzer</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Michigan Alcoholism Screening Test (MAST): preliminary report</article-title><source>Univ. Mich. Med. Cent. J.</source><year>1968</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>143</fpage><lpage>145</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5662860</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR20"><label>20.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flannery</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Volpicelli</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Pettinati</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychometric properties of the Penn Alcohol Craving Scale</article-title><source>Alcohol Clin. Exp. Res.</source><year>1999</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>1289</fpage><lpage>1295</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10470970</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR21"><label>21.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fagerstrom</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Heatherton</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Koslowski</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nicotine addiction and its assessment</article-title><source>Ear Nose Throat J.</source><year>1991</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>763</fpage><lpage>765</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR22"><label>22.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berger</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Ethyl glucuronide in hair and fingernails as a long-term alcohol biomarker</article-title><source>Addiction</source><year>2014</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>425</fpage><lpage>431</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">24524319</pub-id></elem